2025/11/18 K.Fujii original version
2025/12/06 K.Fujii revised
2026/02/19 J.Tian revised & independently tested with all steps

0) How to install external libraries for lcsoft 
0-0a) expand the lcinstall package
$ cd ~
$ mkdir -p sandbox
$ pushd sandbox
$ tar -zxvf <somewhere>/lcinstall.tar.gz 
.......
$ ls
lcinstall
$ ls lcinstall
README
SRPMS
lcsoft.tar.gz
setup-physsim.sh


0-0b) set up your rpmbuild environment
$ cd ~
$ mkdir -p rpmbuild/{BUILD,BUILDROOT,SOURCES,SPECS,SRPMS,RPMS/x86_64}
$ cd rpmbuild/SPECS
$ mkdir -p tmp/done
$ cd tmp
$ cp -a ~/sandbox/lcinstall/SRPMS/* .
$ mkdir ~/sw


0-1) pythia/v6.428 to build root5/whizard
$ pwd
<your home directory>/rpmbuild/SPECS/tmp
$ rpm -i pythia-6.428-kekcc2c.src.rpm
$ cd ..
$ mkdir LOGs
$ rpmbuild -ba pythia6.spec --nodebuginfo >& LOGs/pythia6 &
$ tail -f LOGs/pythia6 
...
CTRL+C
$ ls ../RPMS/x86_64/
pythia-6.428-kekcc2c.x86_64.rpm
$ cd tmp
$ mkdir temp
$ cd temp
$ rpm2cpio ../../../RPMS/x86_64/pythia-6.428-kekcc2c.x86_64.rpm | cpio -id
$ ls
home  usr
$ mv home/<your user id>/sw/pythia ~/sw/
$ cd ..
$ rm -rf temp
$ mv pythia-6.428-kekcc2c.src.rpm done/


